            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Tag textobject in 'mini.ai' is implemented via Lua patterns, which [can result in false positives](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L45-L46).\r\n\r\nThis particular case is due to the fact that built-in `t` textobject only considers tags that contain only alphanumeric characters as their name. The `motion.h1` contains `.`.  The #2057 proposed to include the dot by default, but [my suggestion](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2057#issuecomment-3393500769) is to invest into setting up `t` textobject that uses tree-sitter parser for a more robust experience.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Tag textobject in 'mini.ai' is implemented via Lua patterns, which <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/b409fd1d8b9ea7ec7c0923eb2562b52ed5d1ab0a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L45-L46\">can result in false positives</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This particular case is due to the fact that built-in <code class=\"notranslate\">t</code> textobject only considers tags that contain only alphanumeric characters as their name. The <code class=\"notranslate\">motion.h1</code> contains <code class=\"notranslate\">.</code>.  The <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3506110225\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2057\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2057/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2057\">#2057</a> proposed to include the dot by default, but <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2057#issuecomment-3393500769\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2057/hovercard\">my suggestion</a> is to invest into setting up <code class=\"notranslate\">t</code> textobject that uses tree-sitter parser for a more robust experience.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Tag textobject in 'mini.ai' is implemented via Lua patterns, which can result in false positives.\nThis particular case is due to the fact that built-in t textobject only considers tags that contain only alphanumeric characters as their name. The motion.h1 contains ..  The #2057 proposed to include the dot by default, but my suggestion is to invest into setting up t textobject that uses tree-sitter parser for a more robust experience.",
